  "notes": [
    "Four write keys, not three: the Firebase catalog and commands have create, approve, supersede and retire. A first version asks create; a version that names a predecessor asks supersede (functions/src/performance/performanceGoalCommands.ts, createPerformanceGoalDraft). Mirroring only three would remove \"replace a target in force\".",
    "performance.goal.read is already granted by migration 1764650000000 (twelve Roles) and is not part of this change.",
    "No Firebase holder of these keys is scoped or conditioned (scopesByPermission / conditionsByPermission name none of them), so every EOS grant is flat. Reach is decided by the command, per scope type, exactly as the goal reads decide it.",
    "admin and owner hold the whole catalog by derivation (ADMIN_ROLE composes PERMISSION_CATALOG; owner composes admin), which is why they appear; DECISIONS #162's prose also lists purchasingManager, but the compiled catalog grants it none of the four. The catalog is the authority, so purchasingManager receives nothing.",
    "salesperson, partsAssociate, warehouseAssociate and performanceGoalSubject hold performance.goal.read only: they cannot author, approve or retire a target."
  ]
